988 samples, 60 materials, novel-material split holds out 12

==============================================================================
A. RANK SENSITIVITY — is 64 modes hiding a representation limit?
==============================================================================
   modes    POD floor   rf novel-mat    ratio
  --------------------------------------------
       8   1.4759e-02         0.0496     3.4x   [9s]
      16   7.3249e-03         0.0492     6.7x   [13s]
      32   3.4929e-03         0.0492    14.1x   [19s]
      64   1.4554e-03         0.0492    33.8x   [33s]
     128   5.4592e-04         0.0492    90.2x   [107s]

  POD floor falls 27.0x from 8 to 128 modes (basis improves a lot)
  arm error falls 1.01x over the same range
  => arm error is FLAT in rank. The basis is not the constraint.
     L1's diagnosis holds: it is a learning failure. L2 is the right next rung.

