        2  [12, 15, 23, 24, ...]   1.469e-03     0.0503   34.2x
        3    [1, 5, 10, 11, ...]   1.514e-03     0.0539   35.6x
        4     [0, 3, 4, 10, ...]   1.420e-03     0.0495   34.8x

  rf novel-material error across splits: 0.0502 +- 0.0019  (min 0.0483, max 0.0539)
  gap above floor:                       32.2x +- 4.5x
  => the conclusion is stable across holdout sets. L1 is not a fluke of one split.

